pySMESH: PolygonPerFace_2D builds the ViscousLayers2D it is given (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: PolygonPerFace_2D with a ViscousLayers2D hypothesis builds the layer quadrangles and
then fails the FACE with "Less that 3 nodes on the wire", the layer cells left in the mesh. A
ViscousLayers2D hypothesis assigned on the FACE itself is refused as incompatible.

Symptom: the unit square, Regular_1D with 4 segments, PolygonPerFace_2D, ViscousLayers2D (0.3
thick, 3 layers) on one edge: "Less that 3 nodes on the wire". The same through the
PolygonPerFace_2D inside PolyhedronPerSolid_3D, with the layers on a face of a box.

Root cause: Compute builds the layers (StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D::Compute, :85) and takes the
wire through the proxy mesh, whose EDGEs with layers, and EDGEs that the layers shrank, are
proxy sub-meshes. It reads the wire with StdMeshers_FaceSide::GetOrderedNodes() (:97). For a
proxy sub-mesh, GetOrderedNodes() keys each point by the previous EDGEs' share of the wire plus
the point's normalized parameter on its own EDGE, neither scaled to the EDGE's share nor
oriented (StdMeshers_FaceSide.cxx:708-714), unlike GetUVPtStruct(), which does both (:540-559)
and counts the proxy points (:415-424). The keys collide, the count check then clears the list
(:786-791), and Compute finds no node. The hypothesis is also missing from the compatible list,
and CheckHypothesis accepts everything without the layer check. The algorithm is from SMESH
fe7d1d576 (2015-06-30, "23070: [CEA 1502] Create the 2D mesh from the 1D mesh with one mesh
face for each geom face"); upstream master at 83f8bf482 (2026-09-14) has the same code.
GetOrderedNodes() is not changed here: six other algorithms call it.

Change, in StdMeshers_PolygonPerFace_2D.cxx only:
* the constructor lists ViscousLayers2D as compatible, as Quadrangle_2D does (:101);
* CheckHypothesis runs StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D::CheckHypothesis, as Quadrangle_2D does
  (:200);
* Compute reads a wire that holds a proxy sub-mesh with GetUVPtStruct().

Not changed: a FACE with no ViscousLayers2D: its wire has no proxy sub-mesh and is read with
GetOrderedNodes() as before, and CheckHypothesis finds no layer hypothesis, so its mesh is the
same, bit for bit.

